 When either is wired up, the field stops being dead and the corresponding `#[allow]` can be removed.
+
+## Smells left by the `cached_logs.block_timestamp` change (unsmell run, 2026-11-01)
+
+Found while cleaning up the per-log timestamp change. None was fixed in that run: each one either sits on lines the change did not touch or needs a larger refactor.
+
+### Log cache (`src/evm/cache/log_cache.rs`, `src/evm/cache.rs`)
+
+- **`insert_logs` selects and writes in one loop** (`log_cache.rs`, `insert_logs`). The loop skips pending logs, applies the `unwrap_or(0)` defaults, encodes the row and runs `execute`, all in the same body. Fix: filter the logs that have a `block_hash` first, encode each into a named row struct (the counterpart of `row_to_log`), then run the inserts over the result. That struct should also own the column list: today `log_columns!`, the `?1 … ?13` placeholders, the `params!` order and the names in `row_to_log` must still agree by hand.
+- **No parsed "mined log" type** (`log_cache.rs:insert_logs`, `history.rs:log_to_evm_event` and `log_timestamp`). The optional fields of alloy's `Log` are read again at each use. A missing `block_number`, `log_index` or `transaction_index` silently becomes 0. A missing `block_hash` is skipped by the cache but turned into `[0; 32]` by `log_to_evm_event`. `transaction_hash` is bound as an `Option` into a `NOT NULL` column, so a log without one fails the whole batch. Fix: parse each RPC log once into a `MinedLog` type that both files take.
+- **The u64↔i64 SQLite casts are written about 20 times.** Fix: two named helpers (or a `ToSql`/`FromSql` newtype for block numbers and timestamps).
+- **`CACHE_VERSION` doc contradicts the migrations** (`cache.rs:36`). It says to bump the version on every schema change, but schema changes go through `migrations()` without a bump. Fix: say that the version is bumped only for changes a migration cannot express.
+- **`BlockHeader` uses primitives** (`log_cache.rs:72-76`). `timestamp` is a bare `u64` instead of `arch::Timestamp`, and `hash`/`parent_hash` are `[u8; 32]`. `insert_block_header` takes the four fields loose, and `history.rs:ensure_block_header_via` unpacks a header to call it and then rebuilds one. Fix: type the fields and make `insert_block_header` take `&BlockHeader`.
+- **No filter type.** `address: [u8; 20]` and `topics: [Option<[u8; 32]>; 4]` travel together through `compute_filter_hash`, `EvmLogHistory::with_options`, `build_fetcher` and `apply_topics`, and the filter hash is a bare `[u8; 32]` next to block hashes of the same type. Fix: a `LogFilter { address, topics }` with `hash() -> FilterHash` and `apply(Filter)`.
+- **`match rows.next() { Some(r) => Ok(Some(r?)), None => Ok(None) }` is written twice** (`get_log_by_ref`, `get_block_header`). Use rusqlite's `OptionalExtension`, as `src/matcher/anchor_store_sqlite.rs` already does.
+- **`(SELECT block_hash FROM reorged_blocks)` is spelled four times**, and the scanned-range INSERT twice. Name them once.
+- **`compact_ranges` merges intervals inline.** Extract an interval-merge helper with its own tests.
+- **`CacheDb::open` and `open_in_memory` have the same body.**
+- **Blob decoding panics on a bad length** (`copy_from_slice` in `row_to_log` and `get_block_header`). Return a decode error instead.
+- **Docs.** The module and type docs list the tables (four copies), and "navigation queries live in `LogIndex`" is said three times. The docs of `get_log_by_ref`, `record_scanned_range`, `invalidate_from` and similar state caller preconditions ("the caller is expected to…", "Only call this…") instead of a contract. `get_logs_in_range`'s doc has no verb. `arch.md:256` still says `LogStore`.
+
+### History (`src/evm/history.rs`)
+
+- **`provider` and `store` are threaded into every header lookup** (`ensure_block_header_via`, `log_timestamp`, the `iter` closure, `build_fetcher`). Fix: a `HeaderSource { provider, store }` with `header(block)` and `timestamp_of(&Log)` methods, the latter replacing the free `log_timestamp`. At the same time, give `ensure_block_header_via` an error contract (its doc narrates "cache-first, falls back to RPC") and narrow it from `pub(crate)`, since it has no caller outside this file.
+- **The fetcher repeats header lookups.** `blocks_needing_header` yields the same block once per log, so a block with many logs is looked up many times. Dedupe the block numbers before the loop. The fetcher closure also mixes filter-building detail with its steps, and the `Filter` is built the same way in two places.
+- **`EvmPosition::new(b, u32::MAX)` is the end-of-block cut, written about 12 times.** Fix: `EvmPosition::end_of_block(b)`.
+- **`self_ref: OnceLock<Weak<Self>>` is set after construction.** `Arc::new_cyclic` removes the temporal coupling.
+- **`with_options` takes 6 parameters**, two of them adjacent `u64`s (`chunk_size`, `block_time`). `anchor_timestamp` and `block_time` are bare `u64` without a unit.
+- **Smaller repeats:** `get_block_number` with its `map_err` (twice), the boxed warn callback (twice), `evm_to_block_pos` should be a `From` impl, `_unused_warmup` is a dead shim, and the test literals `200u64` and `12` repeat the anchor block and `DEFAULT_BLOCK_TIME`.
+- **Docs.** The module doc is 26 lines and lists mechanisms. `subscribe` and `update_tip` name no errors, and `subscribe` does not mention the task it spawns. Line 218 lists callers. Line 197 is imperative, and line 243 starts with "Internal:".
+
+### Tests
+
+- **`make_test_log` (`log_cache.rs`) and `make_log` (`history.rs`) build the same `Log`.** Share one test fixture.
